      "source": [
        "The fixed-spectrum construction differs from the hidden-determinant-sign construction in Section 3 and Appendix B.",
        "Normalizer independence of O means pointwise lack of eigenbasis dependence; it does not refer to the independence of O and the algorithm seed.",
        "A is a precision matrix; A^{-1} is the Gaussian covariance. V_A and f_A use the same 1/2 quadratic convention.",
        "Eq11 is a literal definition on its full index carrier, with θ at half-grid points. A zero-based formal index requires an explicit i↔i+1 translation.",
        "Gaussian normalizer means the mass of the unnormalized Lebesgue density, not an integral with respect to the already normalized Gaussian law.",
        "Known given public spectrum is informational, not a new numerical-approximation or query-complexity theorem."
